# Line endings, pinned.
#
# ── WHY THIS FILE EXISTS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This repo has `core.autocrlf = true`, so git stores LF and hands the working tree
# CRLF on checkout. Several tests read a source file raw and match patterns like
# `\n\t\t}` against it — those only match LF, so whether the suite passes depended on
# whether a given file had last been written by an editor (CRLF) or by a tool (LF).
#
# That is a coin flip, and it fails for anyone who clones this fresh. Pinning the
# working tree to LF makes the checkout match what git already stores, so the source a
# test reads is the source everyone else has.
*           text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never translated, never diffed as text.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.zip       binary
*.exe       binary
*.docx      binary
